  "thesis": "Cause, constraint, agency, norm and response differ; causal understanding informs responsibility without dissolving it. Choice-to-necessity laundering hides values and alternatives; constraints narrow choices while compulsion eliminates them. Classification thresholds encode institutional choices and can reshape behavior and confirming data; power requires audit rather than automatic dismissal. Explanation debt is dependency on provisional stories without revalidation; exit costs make correction harder, unlike persistent frameworks repeatedly tested. Dual description combines functional language with lived consequences; understanding a harmful action need not excuse it.",
